<</CreationDate(D:20101202164250Z)/Subject(Disclosed is a wrist mechanism for an industrial robot which includes a first wrist member \(3\) disposed rotatably at the tip of a robot arm \(17\) and a second wrist member \(4\) movable relative to this first wrist member. The movement of the second wr\
ist member \(4\) relative to the first wrist member \(3\) is effected not in a bending mode in which the angle of intersection between the members is variable but in a rotating mode in which the second wrist member \(4\) becomes rotatable. The transmissio\
n of the rotational power to the second wrist member \(4\) is effected through a universal joint \(6, 7\). With this arrangement such backlashes as are conventionally found in the engagement between gears can be reduced, and the mechanical burden on the u\
niversal joint \(6, 7\) can also be reduced.)/PDFVersion(1.4)/Creator(Jouve S.A., TaggedPDF v1.27)/Keywords("EP200202"; "EP 200202"; "B25J 17/00"; "Wrist mechanism for industrial robot")/Producer(Adobe PDF Library 8.0)/ModDate(D:20101214155110+01'00')/Title(Wrist mechanism for industrial robot - European Patent Office - EP 200202 A2)>>
endobj
